<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">I'm Right Where You Left Me</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Catra didnâ€™t want her revenge. She didnâ€™t want to try and stumble her way back to a person that didnâ€™t care about her the same way she had cared. She didnâ€™t want to break her own heart any further. So she stayed. She stayed hidden in the woods, and then later moved to hide in Thaymor where everyone adopted her. But she never left. She stayed in the place where she could relive the most horrible moment of her life every day.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;She stayed right where Adora had left her.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A Canon-Divergent AU told by the perspective of several villagers and by Catraâ€™s own perspective, inspired by Taylor Swiftâ€™s â€œRight Where You Left Meâ€ starting the moment that Adora and Catra separated in Thaymor. Because all of Taylorâ€™s songs can fit Catradora. All of them.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>AOS100</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
